{
 "result": "csvsum.py is a single-pass stdlib body. It reads stdin as bytes, splits on commas and newlines, and groups the val fields by cat in a dict. It converts values to float, sums each group with math.fsum, and writes the sorted \"cat,sum\" lines with 2 decimals. It passes the sample in-0/out-0 check, which runs in about 0.36s on 1M rows. The assay was accepted with baseline 1.74085 and noise 8.5%. I have not tried a faster variant, so the body has no measured gain. I'm resting to keep the remaining energy for the lineage.",
